Expense Tracker Application – Product Documentation

1.Project Overview:--
The Expense Tracker Application is a full-stack web application used to manage daily expenses. 
Users can add, view, update, delete, search, sort, filter, and analyze expenses easily.

The project is developed using:
Python
Streamlit (Frontend)
FastAPI (Backend)
MySQL (Database)

2.Features:
Add Expenses
View Expenses
Update Expenses
Delete Expenses
Search Expenses by Category
Sort Expenses
Filter Expenses
Expense Analysis using Line Chart

3.Technologies used
Technology and Purpose:
Python--->	Used as the core programming language for application development
Streamlit--->	Used to build the interactive frontend user interface
FastAPI	--->Used to develop backend REST APIs
MySQL--->	Used to store and manage expense data
Pandas--->	Used for data processing and displaying tabular data
Requests Library--->	Used for frontend and backend API communication
Uvicorn--->Used to run the FastAPI backend server

4.System Architecture:
User
↓
Streamlit Frontend (User Interface)
↓
Requests Library (API Calls)
↓
FastAPI Backend (REST APIs)
↓
MySQL Database (Data Storage)

5.Database Table:expenses
Column Name	Data Type
expense_id	INT
title	VARCHAR
amount	FLOAT
category	VARCHAR
created_at	TIMESTAMP

6.API Endpoints:
| Method | Endpoint              | Purpose                               |
| ------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| POST   | /add_expense          | Used to add a new expense record      |
| GET    | /ViewExpenses         | Used to retrieve all expense records  |
| PUT    | /update_expense/{id}  | Used to update an existing expense    |
| DELETE | /delete_expenses/{id} | Used to delete an expense record      |
| GET    | /search_expenses      | Used to search expenses by category   |
| GET    | /sort_expenses        | Used to sort expenses based on amount |
| GET    | /filter_expenses      | Used to filter expenses by amount     |

7.Advantages:
Simple UI
Easy expense management
Fast performance
Real-time data handling
Expense visualization

8.Conclusion

The Expense Tracker Application helps users efficiently track and manage expenses using a 
simple and interactive interface. The project demonstrates frontend-backend integration using
Streamlit, FastAPI, and MySQL.
